# Home and Nav Category Filter

The **homepage category carousel** and the **bottom navbar category sheet** (the sheet that opens when the user taps "دسته بندی ها" on mobile) show only categories whose **name** contains at least one of these substrings:

- کیف
- دامن
- کت
- لباس زیر
- شال و روسری
- پیراهن
- شلوار

## Where it is defined

- **Constant**: [frontend/src/constants/categories.ts](mdc:frontend/src/constants/categories.ts) exports `ALLOWED_HOME_NAV_CATEGORY_NAME_SUBSTRINGS` (readonly array). Edit this list to change which categories appear on the homepage carousel and in the bottom nav sheet.
- **Service**: [frontend/src/services/product/categories.ts](mdc:frontend/src/services/product/categories.ts) — `getProductCategories()` accepts optional `allowedNameSubstrings?: readonly string[]`. When provided, the returned list is filtered in-memory so each category’s `name` includes at least one of the substrings.
- **Usage**: Home page passes the constant when fetching categories for the carousel; [BottomNavigation](mdc:frontend/src/components/PLP/BottomNavigation.tsx) uses `useProductCategories({ mainOnly: true, allowedNameSubstrings: ALLOWED_HOME_NAV_CATEGORY_NAME_SUBSTRINGS })`.

## Other category UIs

The **categories page**, **PLP filter**, **CategoriesModal**, and other call sites do **not** pass `allowedNameSubstrings`, so they continue to show all categories (no name filter).
